Z||000000||3.8T Fiero GT||11-16-2001||10:39 PM||||Now i know it sounds like an obvious or dumb question, but does anyone know?  <P>I have plenty of places to go to here in Toronto, but all sell the SAME style rims, mainly to the import market.  I can find my size easy, but I was hoping maybe u guys in the US could show me sumptin I could get shippd here for like under $2500 CDN dollars or less (maybe $1500 USD shipping incl. or so) that look sgood AND is deep dish in the rear?<P>I know the Fiero is a RWD, yet set up like a FWD car so the offset is ok in the rear hence why FWD rims look ok in the rear.  <P>I was wondering if the immitationn Z-06 rims would git it at all, but i figure they are too big...<P>I have seen some of your cars online, i like burgundy cars rims (LT1 choptops other car preview and 1fst2m6 Fiero's rims... for example...I hear porsche rims fit with minor mods too!? true?<P>pics anyone?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cache.ucr.edu/~currie/turbo-t.jpg">  <BR><B>"A 3.8T makes and excellent "RICE" cooker"</B>||||reg||5
