Z||000006||kempo||11-17-2001||12:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 3.8T Fiero GT:<BR><B><BR>and those kumhos are amazing tires, WAY under-rated...i studied them!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just got Kuhmo's on my 17" on the Fiero, and they SUCK!  imo- They are the worst tire I've ever had, and handle like complete and utter crap.  I will never ever buy Kuhmo tires again...  absolute crap.  I have had great experience with Michelin tires, and am trading in my Kuhmo's for the Michelins.  I'll have pics of the 17"s on the fiero tomorrow, look for it in GFC.  Peace.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.admist.net/gtsmall.jpg">    <BR>0-60 6.9 seconds||||reg||13
Z||000007||Adrift||11-17-2001||01:14 AM||||Cheap Thrills - never been there, have been told it IS the place to go though (going wed. morning to buy rims for my car!) Very hard to find info on the place (I've been told to bring cash only - All prices include hardware, PST & GST hehehe) so here it is:<P>Shoot down the 401 west towards london ways (its not far though  ... Exit on Highway 25 in milton, and head south on 25 past the macdonalds, past the opp station... Its on your right hand side (about 1 km off the highway) <P>TEL:905-878-6853 (They answer the phone by saying "6853" not "cheap thrills"<BR>Hours: Mon, Wed, Fri & Saturday. 9-6.<P>Here's the story I've heard: owned by bikers, this place closes down ever winter. Its a Six bay Installation with just walls and walls of tires and rims - they claim to stock for ENkei/Rial and Advanti then the distributors for those brands it Canada! Prices are supposed to be amazing too (I've been told not to try and bargain) Supposedly very Fiero friendly as well...||||reg||1
